#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100733 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101021 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "a0f21b4c-0f5c-5567-aaec-9da481d2e7ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-547" :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100734 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101022 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "0c84fc6d-422e-5729-94d2-a12cda71f78d" :question/math-academy-id "e-548" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100735 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "244bb10c-4c6f-5be0-bd9a-72b4defee245" :question/math-academy-id "e-549" :question/problem "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100736 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "a1572338-79f7-5da7-b9f6-552dcb7984a6" :question/math-academy-id "e-550" :question/problem "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](images/64/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101021 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b0f012-5591-5aff-8da7-43979fdaa3e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458615} {:answer/id #uuid "144f3798-1276-5a78-83a3-816771ac6cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458659} {:answer/id #uuid "406cd5e7-a858-5cc4-950e-6b7acc196782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458748} {:answer/id #uuid "b9eb659e-472e-5762-883d-3f335f4c2bea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458963} {:answer/id #uuid "e63d388e-b33b-5696-a3dc-b3e54fa1e00e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "406cd5e7-a858-5cc4-950e-6b7acc196782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458748} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ec3f5ae-2515-5b2d-8a99-5d2ea67b4ac9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "212286d9-e641-57e0-939d-5fc079361cc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-120317" :question/problem "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+10$ on the interval $[-2,4].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}2{x}^{2}+10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+10x)|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{2\\cdot {4}^{3}}{3}+10\\cdot 4)-(\\frac{2\\cdot (-2)^{3}}{3}+10\\cdot (-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 108 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =18 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}+10 & =18 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =4 \\\\ c & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c3801fa-cab8-5b60-b6f6-7faabc033544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458642} {:answer/id #uuid "20cc8be1-6aad-542c-828d-b26b9f7b09e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458693} {:answer/id #uuid "85c07f8b-9e67-587a-8d6d-5d4b89dc912e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458861} {:answer/id #uuid "ea7298a7-bc34-59b0-9ffe-45c3dccd07f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459038} {:answer/id #uuid "ffae3be5-ba95-5960-879f-25dc2c7ba21b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85c07f8b-9e67-587a-8d6d-5d4b89dc912e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458861} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7077b7e-7107-54d1-b00e-40ddba058261" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d2abb2d-5fae-5b42-8b46-286ab0af6f29" :question/math-academy-id "q-120452" :question/problem "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x-10$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $8.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(3{x}^{2}-6x-10)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & ={\\frac{1}{c}({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-10x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 8 & =\\frac{1}{c}[({c}^{3}-3{c}^{2}-10c)-0] \\\\ 8 & ={c}^{2}-3c-10 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-3c-18 \\\\ 0 & =(c+3)(c-6) \\\\ c & =-3,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $c>0,$ we conclude that $c=6$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14954a9d-42cd-5dc2-aa4a-1b9324477056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458661} {:answer/id #uuid "4c82c965-3218-58e2-86e7-5c97a23e40fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458765} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa501ed-a2a5-587a-ad86-c079c1c6e557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458879} {:answer/id #uuid "d641f85e-932e-5c6e-b393-4e2c37954749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459001} {:answer/id #uuid "fc1fb5e4-8023-5c9f-ae0d-1e5d756de121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14954a9d-42cd-5dc2-aa4a-1b9324477056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458661} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ef3803a-b4c1-5510-80b4-9ed7226dceef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "74a8d294-acf0-5af3-a3bb-298803beabab" :question/math-academy-id "q-120721" :question/problem "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=9{x}^{2}+6x-18$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(9{x}^{2}+6x-18)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-18x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(3{c}^{3}+3{c}^{2}-18c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =3{c}^{2}+3c-18 \\\\ 0 & =(c+3)(3c-6) \\\\ c & =-3,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $c>0,$ we conclude that $c=2$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65614953-9457-5635-b00f-7cb8e99243a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458808} {:answer/id #uuid "6931786b-7b48-5b7f-9f63-304f87a4cab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458813} {:answer/id #uuid "88e6a969-159c-523e-bd83-6aa3909fbdb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458869} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b1cfaa-0cc8-5495-ba4c-467aba53b937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459003} {:answer/id #uuid "f5040f1d-a0fc-52ad-b055-a6d973862e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65614953-9457-5635-b00f-7cb8e99243a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458808} :answer-field/id #uuid "9305964a-cec5-5746-85e7-f3fce14b3137" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "213c9893-b1bb-52cc-a602-24f43ba80406" :question/math-academy-id "q-15237" :question/problem "![](images/97/97b55bafaa70ef2984575a30f06209e11304ff975df689833134fa672fdd7183.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-5,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$, $7$ and $3,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-5,4].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-5+7-3=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-5)}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ecb5918-3d7d-5d46-aea0-d35f67d99fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458650} {:answer/id #uuid "29ae6d76-d2c2-5b42-944d-501a1cafa8d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458709} {:answer/id #uuid "7958ae5e-bfba-588f-b79a-c87119da97f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458844} {:answer/id #uuid "d06d36be-6e65-539b-8210-637fe9bacd84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458990} {:answer/id #uuid "e7861b90-a5d1-521a-ba77-33defd93a904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7958ae5e-bfba-588f-b79a-c87119da97f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458844} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a9c7ed5-2f6c-5ddc-a8f5-9cd3c9b0398b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4039708-ee8a-57dd-b312-f84f190dda62" :question/math-academy-id "q-18135" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cc31e5e85263f5a08a10c73c76cf5ba5eec2c27195159da31ef96a614efba7ed.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-2,4],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments. Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-2,4].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,1].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,4].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =3-3 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a93b98b3-fc61-5f38-b2cf-0e4d0d84697e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098936} {:answer/id #uuid "15bf6613-ed49-5c14-8962-302fba899942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098937} {:answer/id #uuid "2553718f-9dc9-58d5-b044-7b0ec9b75acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098938} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5c77a9-0ae1-5fca-9298-b1a2fbddfb48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098939} {:answer/id #uuid "70c7b215-8a02-5ef3-8a75-f44389330a1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a93b98b3-fc61-5f38-b2cf-0e4d0d84697e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098936} :answer-field/id #uuid "76405eb1-2f74-542e-aab9-001fe5ee76ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "794367ad-cee9-50fc-b4cc-e78beb478cad" :question/math-academy-id "q-18144" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d661fd02727800f40ccaaf7f388b99b61b9e3a2d6c2da351c47b2166d1182b48.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-3,6]$, is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $40$, $20$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,6].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=40-20+10=30.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-3)}\\cdot (30) \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101021 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "083dd1d3-823c-57f9-8184-a1cb578db0ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458631} {:answer/id #uuid "140c121d-05e1-51d2-8431-d9ed6b77a79e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458658} {:answer/id #uuid "44eaebe3-9724-53dd-b799-12daa8d6d031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458753} {:answer/id #uuid "613cb4c6-4d39-53ac-b44d-a72cb678db5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458794} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d3b459-fd7a-5f91-997d-002b313381d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44eaebe3-9724-53dd-b799-12daa8d6d031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458753} :answer-field/id #uuid "a670b852-3ebb-5a3f-af8e-c87a27ff6207" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5dd04ec5-fe77-51e6-b7d8-942237bfd483" :question/math-academy-id "q-2478" :question/problem "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ on the interval $[0,4].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-0}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2})|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3/2}-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{c} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ c & =\\frac{16}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2aa02f-a4ec-550a-ade8-9e48bb5f1850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295716} {:answer/id #uuid "59648138-a114-51e5-892e-a0c2df92248a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295782} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe67af0-fcaf-5d5e-a56d-77eb12803f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296359} {:answer/id #uuid "d38fcd7d-c6b8-55d1-8fad-9a37e56de360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296381} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2eab6a-2a27-5e35-9dc7-aaca0c578fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59648138-a114-51e5-892e-a0c2df92248a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295782} :answer-field/id #uuid "6374f584-b639-5c44-b777-84bde5e5310d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16b1bc24-13e7-5da4-a569-33e3816b732d" :question/math-academy-id "q-30872" :question/problem "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+14x-5$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-6{x}^{2}+14x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-5x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-2{c}^{3}+7{c}^{2}-5c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =-2{c}^{2}+7c-5 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}-7c+5 & =0 \\\\ (c-1)(2c-5) & =0 \\\\ c & =1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101021 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "515b197f-4673-5a1c-a567-0bc1fa171663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "515b197f-4673-5a1c-a567-0bc1fa171663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458772} :answer-field/id #uuid "388db07d-138b-5e93-8934-380434a72117" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c05ccb32-8966-53e4-9d10-3d74a13d9dc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c05ccb32-8966-53e4-9d10-3d74a13d9dc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458975} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee7a1c58-5c7d-5c74-9e8e-4e4a9faebb3c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b16fe381-16d5-5d5d-acea-e99a321f7b25" :question/math-academy-id "q-316284" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the **exact** values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)={x}^{2}+2x$ on the interval $[-3,3]$ are\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,c=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-(-3)}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}+2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2})|}_{-3}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+{3}^{2})-(\\frac{(-3)^{3}}{3}+(-3)^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot [(9+9)-(-9+9)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =3 \\\\ {c}^{2}+2c & =3 \\\\ {c}^{2}+2c-3 & =0 \\\\ (c+1)^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ c+1 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ c & =-3,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem on the interval $[-3,3]$ are \n\n$$\nc=-3,\\,\\text{and}\\,c=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101022 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b36dea13-9c1f-5885-939b-78c3be24015d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{5\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b36dea13-9c1f-5885-939b-78c3be24015d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{5\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458952} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7a35d36-00f8-577a-8dd4-9fb713b96b96" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459156}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ef347b8-64ff-5465-9d5f-8f167a76e412" :question/math-academy-id "q-316298" :question/problem "Find the average value ${g}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $g(x)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x$ on the interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{6}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${g}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{6}{\\pi }(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }[(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}))-(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\cdot 0)+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }[(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(0+0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }[(\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1)-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }(\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{16}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4f22f82-3f4c-56a7-8fca-b1699296b03b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4f22f82-3f4c-56a7-8fca-b1699296b03b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296486} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5ebfc2e-32f9-5714-a71a-21c80776c9ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e5a2c9b-15eb-580e-9b48-bc6a0c515d66" :question/math-academy-id "q-316309" :question/problem "![](images/1c/1c69b5a43e445861a728fcd8faed9e89b3bcb61141ad35d99e60f2a43983244d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-2,9],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(5,0)$ with radius $3.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[0,8].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,8].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8-0}\\cdot (-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101022 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d4f785-6f5a-5ce0-bf69-39aad915511d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{56.5}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302796} {:answer/id #uuid "45450f39-4901-5335-a3d0-7f1c044bd30e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{52.1}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302890} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1d0fe5-2d24-59ed-9880-fe68d2d0d545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{61.2}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302923} {:answer/id #uuid "559548da-50f2-521b-9452-7fc3e2890a87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50.0}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302984} {:answer/id #uuid "782842d2-e11d-5027-8038-91cd35485b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58.9}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "782842d2-e11d-5027-8038-91cd35485b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58.9}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303198} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fac5b99-d1c6-5e15-afc2-0e7b3ba2570b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2e55b4cb-6c56-5cac-893d-482f84ce6bec" :question/math-academy-id "q-3289" :question/problem "During the winter in Pasadena, the temperature, in ${F}^{∘}$, $t$ hours after $9$ a.m. can be modeled by the function $T(t)=50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}).$ Find the average temperature during the period from $9$ a.m. to $9$ p.m." :question/worked-solution "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,12].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12-0}{\\int }_{0}^{12}(50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{12}(50t-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(50\\cdot 12-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 12}{12}))-(50\\cdot 0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{12}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\frac{600\\pi +168}{\\pi }+\\frac{168}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{600\\pi +336}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{600\\pi +336}{12\\pi } \\\\  & ≈{58.9}^{∘}F.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101022 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09d515f9-dbf7-57f9-bfbd-14529adce84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458637} {:answer/id #uuid "2a2d1b64-0409-51ae-8c1b-93e653cb6cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458711} {:answer/id #uuid "788ae64b-69de-5a69-b6ef-695942da8e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458842} {:answer/id #uuid "a3230ad6-8695-5419-99a3-370a4455ae96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458917} {:answer/id #uuid "dadb07b1-259a-5ae6-a2dc-c3cc11186502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a2d1b64-0409-51ae-8c1b-93e653cb6cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458711} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2f0aed6-3b47-526f-ac8a-bfb1cc9f826f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7616dfe0-de8d-5c42-97e8-80147a4d58bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-3292" :question/problem "What is the average value of $g(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ on the interval $[1,8]?$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8-1}{\\int }_{1}^{8}\\sqrt[3]{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4/3})|}_{1}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {8}^{4/3})-(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {1}^{4/3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot ({8}^{1/3})^{4})-\\frac{3}{4}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {2}^{4})-\\frac{3}{4}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 16)-\\frac{3}{4}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}(12-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101022 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34272274-e39f-56d1-b23d-d6f2a622e4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302781} {:answer/id #uuid "4e6335c6-35ae-5399-8646-8a48ae96cd75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302948} {:answer/id #uuid "cedccea5-0ac5-5eb1-b565-b46dfdb1b62d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303733} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f569b4-3616-56ca-b69b-687f426d0093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303884} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4dab3d-a51f-5405-a9a9-031ff453e188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe4dab3d-a51f-5405-a9a9-031ff453e188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304056} :answer-field/id #uuid "08f23813-1ba2-570a-ae16-39c39c5747d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24f38454-bd1c-55d7-83bd-a807c36fe3b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-3297" :question/problem "Within  the interval $[0,\\pi ]$, determine the average value of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\pi ))-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)-(-2\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(\\frac{5}{2})-(-\\frac{3}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459232 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101021 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f118372-3e76-5902-b982-2afdbba7d4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f118372-3e76-5902-b982-2afdbba7d4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458878} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f13fd49-c687-54ea-8567-adb648e4658b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d28c5d8d-8600-597a-be4c-57527d9ced06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d28c5d8d-8600-597a-be4c-57527d9ced06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458995} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5795ec6-b1b2-5702-9bab-bc09c1c1ac74" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4549174b-8bf8-5249-ad67-6ec2c93dbb2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-344540" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the **exact** values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)={x}^{2}-4x$ on the interval $[0,3]$ are\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,c=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-0}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}-4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-2{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}-2\\cdot {3}^{2})-(\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}-2\\cdot {0}^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [(9-18)-(0-0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-9) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =-3 \\\\ {c}^{2}-4c & =-3 \\\\ {c}^{2}-4c+3 & =0 \\\\ (c-2)^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ c-2 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ c & =1,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem on the interval $[0,3]$ are \n\n$$\nc=1,\\,\\text{and}\\,c=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101021 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0462c5a-e194-5968-aa3c-30b604665076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln(2)}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0462c5a-e194-5968-aa3c-30b604665076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln(2)}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458912} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8ca3de3-8094-51d4-be18-d519acf04d79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2fa558e-45d2-5d75-8de8-3dcedde3e30f" :question/math-academy-id "q-344550" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x+1}$ on the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b-a)f(c) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{1-0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{1}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+1))-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0+1))] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ \\frac{1}{c+1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ c+1 & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\ c & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459276 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e99ef6aa-9780-540f-a554-9722d741c35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e99ef6aa-9780-540f-a554-9722d741c35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459036} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aa408c5-0480-57fc-a84a-a8722dbd9190" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459129} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263c317c-832b-5729-b5e0-86f049d2eebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "263c317c-832b-5729-b5e0-86f049d2eebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458706} :answer-field/id #uuid "86f27028-72c3-5e2d-b122-e18e9b55f108" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b4a78cea-04c5-5a3c-8466-a049995b5873" :question/math-academy-id "q-344594" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the **exact** values of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-2x-6$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $6$ are\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and  $\\,c=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(3{x}^{2}-2x-6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & ={\\frac{1}{c}({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-6x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c}[({c}^{3}-{c}^{2}-6c)-0] \\\\ 6c & ={c}^{3}-{c}^{2}-6c \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{3}-{c}^{2}-12c \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-c-12 \\\\ 0 & =(c-4)(c+3) \\\\ c & =-3,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in **ascending order**, the values of $c$ are \n\n$$\nc=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,c=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e836b11-ea3c-54ba-83c6-c7cfd25ab073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e836b11-ea3c-54ba-83c6-c7cfd25ab073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458906} :answer-field/id #uuid "f941bfd8-147c-56b4-bdae-a7b1d8dbf539" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5043abb-6077-57ce-a472-1083e29053c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-344604" :question/problem "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=9\\sqrt{x}+2$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $11$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 11 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(9\\sqrt{x}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 11 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(6{x}^{3/2}+2x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 11 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(6{c}^{3/2}+2c)-0] \\\\ 11 & =6\\sqrt{c}+2 \\\\ 9 & =6\\sqrt{c} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & =\\sqrt{c} \\\\ c & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101022 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "244c1d8b-d2e8-5d24-8f75-383e240735c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "244c1d8b-d2e8-5d24-8f75-383e240735c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458700} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8b7040b-1c28-5651-827d-d9a23db3b9d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "280ecae1-be4d-57a7-89a2-e0f1aff5f58a" :question/math-academy-id "q-344694" :question/problem "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ on the interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3}{\\pi }(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da595137-9f37-5a27-a95e-0bbab8d76644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da595137-9f37-5a27-a95e-0bbab8d76644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459011} :answer-field/id #uuid "63fd8625-d5b1-5940-80d0-afc4cdf67f3a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cdb68157-b846-5747-a6b0-cb5c936a1bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-344714" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9d12008688f8cded02aff352773323ce6b4b8a978746b720ebcba319b7b71598.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-5,5],$ is shown above. It consists of line segments.\n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[-4,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,0].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,4].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-4-6 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-4)}\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
